{"version":3,"createdAt":1791627273272,"mainModel":{"schemaVersion":8,"id":"cm_mv28iv0q","key":"cm_mv28iv0q","name":"Planchard Chapter2 - review Q1-Q15 - browser 2026-10-10","kind":"part","authoringMode":"fully-parametric","localFrame":{"origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0},"yAxis":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0},"zAxis":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}},"references":[{"id":"origin","type":"origin","name":"Origin","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:top","type":"plane","name":"Top Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:front","type":"plane","name":"Front Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:right","type":"plane","name":"Right Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}},{"id":"axis:x","type":"axis","name":"X Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"axis:y","type":"axis","name":"Y Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0}},{"id":"axis:z","type":"axis","name":"Z Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}}],"parameters":{},"sketches":[{"id":"sk_1y8s5","name":"X·Z sketch","plane":"top","offset":0,"referenceId":"plane:top","points":[],"entities":[],"constraints":[],"diagnostics":[],"status":"fully-defined"}],"features":[],"history":[],"parts":[],"assemblies":[],"appearances":[],"notes":[],"markups":[],"rules":{},"metadata":{"authoringSystem":"parametric-v1"},"topologyBindings":[],"namedSelections":[],"revision":1,"lastRebuild":{"ok":true,"signature":"{\"definitionId\":\"cm_mv28iv0q\",\"features\":[],\"history\":[{\"id\":\"history:sketch:sk_1y8s5\",\"kind\":\"sketch\",\"suppressed\":false,\"targetId\":\"sk_1y8s5\"}],\"overrides\":{},\"revision\":1,\"sketches\":[{\"constraints\":[],\"entities\":[],\"id\":\"sk_1y8s5\",\"name\":\"X·Z sketch\",\"offset\":0,\"plane\":\"top\",\"points\":[],\"referenceId\":\"plane:top\"}]}","issues":[],"rebuiltAt":1791627266047},"price":500,"col":"#c9bfae","constraints":[],"rollback":null,"activeSketch":"sk_1y8s5","variables":[],"referenceGeometry":[],"definitionId":"cm_mv28iv0q","documentVersion":1,"context":{"kind":"part","units":{"length":"mm","angle":"deg","mass":"kg","precision":3},"activeCoordinateSystemId":"origin"},"customProperties":{"Description":"Independent Chapter2 review Q1-Q15, source printed2-37/PDF123. Multiview projection, object/hidden/center lines, drawing standards, required projection-symbol outlines are on a separately authored companion sheet. No publisher answer-key, new solid or certification claim."},"drawing":{"version":1,"draftingStandard":"custom","secondaryUnits":"","secondaryPrecision":2,"size":"A3","orientation":"landscape","projection":"third","units":"mm","scale":"fit","showHidden":true,"showCenters":true,"showZones":true,"views":[],"dims":[],"notes":[{"id":"nlxuu849","x":34.755904449194375,"y":24.64126801587906,"text":"CHAPTER2 - REVIEW ANSWERS Q1-Q15\nSource: printed2-37 / PDF123, Planchard2021.\nIndependent explanations; required symbols on companion.\nNo official answer-key, authored CAD or certification claim.","leader":null},{"id":"ncpa4e83","x":34.755904449194375,"y":59.6884669389522,"text":"Q1 - Projection divisions\nAxonometric,Oblique,Perspective.","leader":null},{"id":"n3onsl0t","x":34.755904449194375,"y":71.70465047459105,"text":"Q2 - Axonometric types\nIsometric,Dimetric,Trimetric: three equal axis scales,two equal scales,or\nthree different scales respectively.","leader":null},{"id":"nld8mkd1","x":34.755904449194375,"y":87.22556031987155,"text":"Q3 - Oblique front\nTrue. The front face is drawn in true shape/size; depth recedes obliquely.","leader":null},{"id":"npoyy4l6","x":34.755904449194375,"y":99.2417438555104,"text":"Q4 - Oblique types\nCavalier and Cabinet. Cavalier uses full receding depth; Cabinet uses half\ndepth to reduce apparent distortion.","leader":null},{"id":"nzid5f0a","x":34.755904449194375,"y":114.7626537007909,"text":"Q5 - Perspective\nProjection rays converge at a viewpoint; parallel directions may converge\nto vanishing points and distant features appear smaller. Example: railway\ntracks receding toward the horizon.","leader":null},{"id":"n6ztolv8","x":34.755904449194375,"y":133.78827152047208,"text":"Q6 - One view for uniform parts\nTrue when one view plus dimensions/notes completely defines the part, e.g.a\nsimple turned cylindrical part with diameter and length. Complex geometry\nstill needs additional views.","leader":null},{"id":"nujwkvrg","x":34.755904449194375,"y":152.81388934015325,"text":"Q7 - Front chosen by description\nTrue. Use the view that best describes general shape; it need not coincide\nwith the assembly's installed front.","leader":null},{"id":"nijfwnm0","x":34.755904449194375,"y":168.33479918543378,"text":"Q8 - Diameter symbol\nTrue. Prefix the cylindrical diameter withØ; the OCR's0 is a\ndiameter-symbol substitution, not the numeral zero.","leader":null},{"id":"n3c3p754","x":225.01213765172912,"y":59.6884669389522,"text":"Q9 - Third-angle symbol\nDraw the standard truncated-cone side view plus its aligned\nconcentric-circle end view in third-angle arrangement. The actual source\nPDF102/2-16 draws the frustum with larger end at RIGHT,smaller end at\nLEFT,and the concentric-circle end view at LEFT. Include the center axis.\nThis is a required paper diagram,not a text-only closure.","leader":null},{"id":"npq00lzs","x":225.01213765172912,"y":85.7235373779167,"text":"Q10 - First-angle symbol\nUse the same source frustum orientation,larger end RIGHT and smaller end\nLEFT,but put its concentric-circle end view at RIGHT for first-angle\narrangement. Include the center axis. This is a required paper diagram.","leader":null},{"id":"n7k3rx3s","x":225.01213765172912,"y":104.74915519759787,"text":"Q11 - Angle convention difference\nFirst:object between viewer and plane,Top below/Right left. Third:plane\nbetween viewer and object,Top above/Right right.","leader":null},{"id":"nv11y6tf","x":225.01213765172912,"y":120.27006504287839,"text":"Q12 - US first angle\nFalse under the book's US third-angle convention.","leader":null},{"id":"n4tau1h0","x":225.01213765172912,"y":132.28624857851722,"text":"Q13 - Section hatches\nTrue. Conventional patterns may indicate material families; they are not a\nsubstitute for exact material specification.","leader":null},{"id":"n60sn30q","x":225.01213765172912,"y":147.80715842379774,"text":"Q14 - Mechanical dimension endings\nTrue under the source mechanical-drafting convention, with architectural\nslash/dot exceptions kept separate.","leader":null},{"id":"nbwysoa3","x":225.01213765172912,"y":163.32804993383726,"text":"Q15 - Break lines example\nTrue. They delimit a removed/omitted portion, e.g.a long shaft shortened to\nfit the sheet or a local broken-out region exposing an interior feature.","leader":null}],"primitives":[],"title":{"revision":"A","sheet":1,"sheets":1,"title":"CHAPTER2 - REVIEW Q1-Q15","number":"PLANCHARD2-37-PDF123","author":"","company":"","material":"","finish":"","mass":"","date":"2026-10-10","tolerance":""},"seeded":true},"lastStandardsAudit":{"at":1791627255829,"ok":true,"checked":0,"blocking":[]},"exactTopologyCache":{}},"assemblies":[],"drawings":[],"metadata":{"generator":"ModelForge CAD SolidWorks-Class","units":"mm","attachmentStorage":"content-addressed","activeDocument":{"type":"part","key":"cm_mv28iv0q"}},"attachments":[]}